{"black_box_warning":{"current_value":"No FDA boxed warning identified in selected current DailyMed label.","fda_source_urls":["https://api.fda.gov/drug/label.json?search=openfda.brand_name%3A%22VIMPAT%22&limit=10","https://api.fda.gov/drug/label.json?search=openfda.brand_name%3A%22MOTPOLY%20XR%22&limit=10","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/216185s001lbl.pdf"],"proposed_value":"No FDA boxed warning identified in selected current FDA/openFDA labels for lacosamide (Vimpat/Motpoly XR).","rationale":"The no-boxed-warning conclusion is plausible, but the current row relies on DailyMed, which is not permissible for this field. FDA/openFDA or Drugs@FDA/FDA label sources should be used instead.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"incorrect"},"blocking_questions":[],"fact_checks":[{"current_value":"generic_name=lacosamide; trade_names=Motpoly XR; Vimpat; alternate_generic_names=; pubmed_search_aliases=SPM 927","field":"names_and_aliases","proposed_value":"generic_name=lacosamide; trade_names=Motpoly XR; Vimpat; alternate_generic_names=; pubmed_search_aliases=SPM 927; harkoseride; ADD 234037","rationale":"Lacosamide and the US trade names Vimpat and Motpoly XR are verified. LACOSAMIDE should not be added as a trade name because it is the generic name. PubMed/NCBI literature identifies SPM 927, harkoseride, and ADD 234037 as prior/development aliases; SPM 927 is present but harkoseride and ADD 234037 are missing.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"missing","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/216185s001lbl.pdf","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/?term=17461888"]},{"current_value":"available_in_us=Yes; filter_availability=Available in US; year_fda_cleared=2008; epilepsy_type=Focal; Primary generalized tonic-clonic; filter_epilepsy_type=Focal; Primary generalized tonic-clonic","field":"availability_indications_year","proposed_value":"No change.","rationale":"FDA labeling verifies US availability, Initial U.S. Approval 2008, treatment of partial-onset seizures, and adjunctive treatment of primary generalized tonic-clonic seizures.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/216185s001lbl.pdf","https://api.fda.gov/drug/label.json?search=openfda.generic_name%3A%22LACOSAMIDE%22&limit=10"]},{"current_value":"formulations_available=Tablet; oral solution; IV injection; extended-release capsule; filter_formulation=Capsule; IV/IM injection; Liquid; Long acting; Tablet","field":"formulations_available/filter_formulation","proposed_value":"formulations_available=Tablet; oral solution; IV injection; extended-release capsule; filter_formulation=Capsule; IV injection; Liquid; Long acting; Tablet","rationale":"FDA labeling supports tablets, oral solution, IV injection, and extended-release capsules. The detailed formulation is IV only; IM injection is not supported by the FDA label.","requires_user_approval":true,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/216185s001lbl.pdf","https://api.fda.gov/drug/label.json?search=openfda.brand_name%3A%22VIMPAT%22&limit=10"]},{"current_value":"maximum_approved_daily_dose=400 mg/day; minimum_effective_dose=200 mg/day; typical_doses_per_day=Adults: 200-400 mg/day; IR divided BID or XR once daily","field":"dose_fields","proposed_value":"No change.","rationale":"FDA labeling verifies adult maintenance dosing of 200-400 mg/day for adjunctive therapy, maximum recommended adult dosage 400 mg/day, IR twice-daily dosing, and Motpoly XR once-daily dosing.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/216185s001lbl.pdf","https://api.fda.gov/drug/label.json?search=openfda.brand_name%3A%22VIMPAT%22&limit=10"]},{"current_value":"adverse_symptoms_percentages=CNS: dizziness 23-25%, CNS: somnolence 17%, CNS: headache 14%, GI: nausea 10%, ophthalmologic: diplopia 10%, cardiac: PR prolongation <1%","field":"adverse_symptoms_percentages","proposed_value":"CNS: dizziness 23-25%, CNS: somnolence 17%, CNS: headache 14%, GI: nausea 10%, ophthalmologic: diplopia 10%, cardiac: first-degree AV block 0.4%; dose-dependent PR interval prolongation","rationale":"The CNS/GI/ophthalmologic percentages are supported across FDA-labeled adult partial-onset and PGTC trial data. The cardiac percentage is specifically asymptomatic first-degree AV block 0.4%; PR interval prolongation is a pharmacodynamic effect, not an adverse-event percentage of <1%.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/216185s001lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"qt_interval_effect=No QT prolongation; can prolong PR interval; filter_qt_effect=PR interval effect; QT prolongation","field":"qt_interval_effect/filter_qt_effect","proposed_value":"qt_interval_effect=No QT prolongation; can prolong PR interval; filter_qt_effect=PR interval effect","rationale":"FDA labeling states lacosamide did not prolong QTc and produced a small dose-related PR interval increase. The filter value QT prolongation directly contradicts the label.","requires_user_approval":true,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/216185s001lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"enzyme_inducing_or_inhibiting=Not a clinically meaningful enzyme inducer/inhibitor; filter_enzyme_effect=Inducer; Inhibitor","field":"enzyme_inducing_or_inhibiting/filter_enzyme_effect","proposed_value":"enzyme_inducing_or_inhibiting=Not a clinically meaningful enzyme inducer/inhibitor; filter_enzyme_effect=None","rationale":"FDA labeling and NCBI sources support no clinically meaningful induction/inhibition. The filter value Inducer; Inhibitor directly contradicts the row fact and source evidence.","requires_user_approval":true,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/216185s001lbl.pdf","https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK547940/","https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK493589/"]},{"current_value":"major_organ_for_metabolism=Liver and renal excretion; half_life_range=13 h; filter_metabolism=Liver/hepatic; Renal/no major metabolism","field":"metabolism_half_life","proposed_value":"major_organ_for_metabolism=Liver metabolism and renal excretion; half_life_range=13 h; filter_metabolism=Liver/hepatic; Renal excretion","rationale":"FDA labeling verifies renal excretion plus biotransformation, CYP3A4/CYP2C9/CYP2C19 involvement, and half-life about 13 hours. The phrase Renal/no major metabolism is misleading because lacosamide undergoes hepatic biotransformation.","requires_user_approval":true,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/216185s001lbl.pdf","https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK547940/"]},{"current_value":"mechanism_of_action=Human antiseizure mechanism remains incompletely elucidated; lacosamide selectively enhances slow inactivation of voltage-gated sodium channels and stabilizes hyperexcitable neuronal membranes.; mechanism_confidence=Moderate; mechanism_source=FDA/DailyMed labeling; mechanism_source_tier=FDA label; filter_mechanism=Sodium channel","field":"mechanism_fields","proposed_value":"mechanism_of_action unchanged; mechanism_confidence=Moderate; mechanism_source=FDA labeling; mechanism_source_tier=FDA label; filter_mechanism=Sodium channel","rationale":"Mechanism wording is supported by FDA labeling. Source text should be changed from FDA/DailyMed labeling to FDA labeling to match trusted-source policy.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/216185s001lbl.pdf","https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK493589/"]},{"current_value":"evidence_sources=NCBI LiverTox anticonvulsants table; Epilepsy Society ASM list; Epilepsy Foundation Australia ASM list; FDA/DailyMed labeling","field":"evidence_sources","proposed_value":"FDA/accessdata FDA labeling; FDA/openFDA drug label API; NCBI LiverTox; NCBI Medical Genetics Summaries; PubMed RCT abstracts; ClinicalTrials.gov trial records","rationale":"The current evidence_sources field names DailyMed and non-trusted epilepsy-list sources. Retained facts can be supported by FDA/openFDA/accessdata, NCBI, PubMed, and ClinicalTrials.gov sources instead.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/216185s001lbl.pdf","https://api.fda.gov/drug/label.json?search=openfda.generic_name%3A%22LACOSAMIDE%22&limit=10","https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK547940/","https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK493589/"]},{"current_value":"status_or_notes=Current ASM for focal seizures; also used for primary generalized tonic-clonic seizures in some approvals.","field":"status_or_notes","proposed_value":"Current ASM indicated for focal seizures and for adjunctive treatment of primary generalized tonic-clonic seizures in FDA-approved labeling.","rationale":"FDA labeling now directly supports both focal/partial-onset seizures and adjunctive PGTC use, so the note can be made more exact.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/216185s001lbl.pdf"]}],"generic_name":"lacosamide","missing_rcts":[],"outcome_checks":[{"current_value":"3.9-21.8 % (Makedonska2024 3.9%; Vossler2020 21.8%; Farkas2019 19.6%; Chung2010 20%; Halasz2009 14.7%; BenMenachem2007 19%)","field":"diff_50_responder_maximum_effective_dose / plot_diff_50_responder_maximum_effective_dose","proposed_value":"No change.","rationale":"Differentials match cited arm values: 41.4-37.5=3.9; 68.1-46.3=21.8; 52.9-33.3=19.6; 38.3-18.3=20.0; 40.5-25.8=14.7; 41-22=19.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/38375995/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/32817358/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/31462582/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/20132285/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/19183227/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/17635557/"]},{"current_value":"3.2-30 % (Makedonska2024 3.2%; Farkas2019 30%; Chung2010 16.5%; Halasz2009 15.9%; BenMenachem2007 29%)","field":"diff_median_pct_change_maximum_effective_dose / plot_diff_median_pct_change_maximum_effective_dose","proposed_value":"15.9-30 % (drug minus placebo median percent-change differential at maximum effective dose/regimen: Farkas2019 lacosamide target weight-based pediatric regimen 30%; Chung2010 lacosamide 400 mg/day 16.5%; Halasz2009 lacosamide 400 mg/day 15.9%; BenMenachem2007 lacosamide 400 mg/day 29%)","rationale":"Farkas, Chung, Halasz, and Ben-Menachem values are true active-minus-placebo median percent-change differentials. Makedonska2024 reports a placebo-adjusted percentage reduction in electrographic focal-seizure ADF, not an arm-specific median percent-change value, so it should not be in a median-percent-change field.","requires_user_approval":true,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/38375995/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/31462582/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/20132285/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/19183227/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/17635557/"]},{"current_value":"14.1 % (Vossler2020 lacosamide up to 12 mg/kg/day or 400 mg/day 14.1%)","field":"diff_seizure_freedom_maximum_effective_dose / plot_diff_seizure_freedom_maximum_effective_dose","proposed_value":"No change.","rationale":"Vossler/FDA review values support 31.3% lacosamide vs 17.2% placebo seizure freedom from PGTC at day 166, differential 14.1%.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/32817358/","https://www.fda.gov/media/144647/download?attachment="]}],"overall_status":"needs_update","proposed_row_updates":[{"current_value":"FDA/DailyMed SPL; status=no_boxed_warning_in_selected_label; setid=9e79b42c-38a3-4b2c-a196-a5a1948250e2; published=May 13, 2026; title=VIMPAT (LACOSAMIDE) TABLET, FILM COATED VIMPAT (LACOSAMIDE) INJECTION VIMPAT (LACOSAMIDE) SOLUTION [UCB, INC.]; url=https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/drugInfo.cfm?setid=9e79b42c-38a3-4b2c-a196-a5a1948250e2","field":"fda_black_box_warning_source","proposed_value":"FDA/openFDA drug label API; status=no_boxed_warning_identified_in_selected_current_fda_labeling; api_urls=https://api.fda.gov/drug/label.json?search=openfda.brand_name%3A%22VIMPAT%22&limit=10 and https://api.fda.gov/drug/label.json?search=openfda.brand_name%3A%22MOTPOLY%20XR%22&limit=10; FDA label reference=https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/216185s001lbl.pdf","reason":"DailyMed is not permissible for boxed-warning verification.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://api.fda.gov/drug/label.json?search=openfda.brand_name%3A%22VIMPAT%22&limit=10","https://api.fda.gov/drug/label.json?search=openfda.brand_name%3A%22MOTPOLY%20XR%22&limit=10","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/216185s001lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"SPM 927","field":"pubmed_search_aliases","proposed_value":"SPM 927; harkoseride; ADD 234037","reason":"NCBI/PubMed review identifies harkoseride and ADD 234037 as prior names/aliases for lacosamide; aliases should not become separate drug rows.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/?term=17461888"]},{"current_value":"FoldvarySchaefer2017 and Rudd2015 included in pubmed_phase_ii_iii_rct_links","field":"pubmed_phase_ii_iii_rct_links","proposed_value":"Makedonska2024|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/38375995/; Vossler2020|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/32817358/; Farkas2019|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/31462582/; Hong2016|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/27669155/; Chung2010|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/20132285/; Halasz2009|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/19183227/; BenMenachem2007|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/17635557/","reason":"FoldvarySchaefer2017 is Phase IV sleepiness/cognition, not phase II/III seizure-efficacy RCT. Rudd2015 is a pooled cardiac safety analysis, not a primary phase II/III placebo-controlled seizure-efficacy RCT report.","requires_user_approval":true,"source_urls":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/28866338/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/25933358/"]},{"current_value":"3.2-30 % (includes Makedonska2024 3.2%)","field":"diff_median_pct_change_maximum_effective_dose","proposed_value":"15.9-30 % (drug minus placebo median percent-change differential at maximum effective dose/regimen: Farkas2019 lacosamide target weight-based pediatric regimen 30%; Chung2010 lacosamide 400 mg/day 16.5%; Halasz2009 lacosamide 400 mg/day 15.9%; BenMenachem2007 lacosamide 400 mg/day 29%)","reason":"Makedonska2024 3.2% is placebo-adjusted electrographic ADF percent reduction, not a median percent-change differential.","requires_user_approval":true,"source_urls":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/38375995/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/31462582/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/20132285/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/19183227/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/17635557/"]},{"current_value":"Makedonska2024|3.2|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/38375995/|255; Farkas2019|30|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/31462582/|338; Chung2010|16.5|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/20132285/|405; Halasz2009|15.9|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/19183227/|485; BenMenachem2007|29|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/17635557/|418","field":"plot_diff_median_pct_change_maximum_effective_dose","proposed_value":"Farkas2019|30|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/31462582/|338; Chung2010|16.5|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/20132285/|405; Halasz2009|15.9|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/19183227/|485; BenMenachem2007|29|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/17635557/|418","reason":"Remove Makedonska2024 from the median-percent-change plot for the same reason as above.","requires_user_approval":true,"source_urls":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/38375995/"]},{"current_value":"Inducer; Inhibitor","field":"filter_enzyme_effect","proposed_value":"None","reason":"FDA labeling supports no clinically meaningful enzyme induction/inhibition; current filter contradicts the fact field.","requires_user_approval":true,"source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/216185s001lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"PR interval effect; QT prolongation","field":"filter_qt_effect","proposed_value":"PR interval effect","reason":"FDA labeling states lacosamide did not prolong QTc and can increase PR interval.","requires_user_approval":true,"source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/216185s001lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Capsule; IV/IM injection; Liquid; Long acting; Tablet","field":"filter_formulation","proposed_value":"Capsule; IV injection; Liquid; Long acting; Tablet","reason":"FDA labeling supports IV injection only, not IM injection.","requires_user_approval":true,"source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/216185s001lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"NCBI LiverTox anticonvulsants table; Epilepsy Society ASM list; Epilepsy Foundation Australia ASM list; FDA/DailyMed labeling","field":"evidence_sources","proposed_value":"FDA/accessdata FDA labeling; FDA/openFDA drug label API; NCBI LiverTox; NCBI Medical Genetics Summaries; PubMed RCT abstracts; ClinicalTrials.gov trial records","reason":"Replaces DailyMed/non-trusted list sources with trusted domains that support the retained facts.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/216185s001lbl.pdf","https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK547940/","https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK493589/"]}],"rct_link_checks":[{"label":"Makedonska2024","pmid":"38375995","proposed_action":"Retain.","rationale":"Drug is lacosamide; randomized 1:1 lacosamide/placebo, double-blind parallel-group pediatric focal-seizure trial; ClinicalTrials.gov record identifies NCT02477839 as Phase 3.","status":"verified","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/38375995/"},{"label":"Vossler2020","pmid":"32817358","proposed_action":"Retain.","rationale":"Drug is lacosamide; double-blind randomized placebo-controlled Phase 3 adjunctive trial for primary generalized tonic-clonic seizures.","status":"verified","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/32817358/"},{"label":"Farkas2019","pmid":"31462582","proposed_action":"Retain.","rationale":"Drug is lacosamide; double-blind randomized placebo-controlled pediatric focal-seizure trial; ClinicalTrials.gov NCT01921205 identifies Phase 3.","status":"verified","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/31462582/"},{"label":"FoldvarySchaefer2017","pmid":"28866338","proposed_action":"Remove from pubmed_phase_ii_iii_rct_links with user approval; optionally retain only as a sleep/cognition tolerability reference elsewhere.","rationale":"PubMed identifies this as Clinical Trial, Phase IV. The endpoint was daytime sleepiness/noninferiority, not a phase II/III placebo-controlled seizure-efficacy RCT.","status":"not_phase_ii_iii","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/28866338/"},{"label":"Hong2016","pmid":"27669155","proposed_action":"Retain.","rationale":"Drug is lacosamide; randomized double-blind placebo-controlled Phase 3 adjunctive trial in Chinese and Japanese adults with partial-onset seizures.","status":"verified","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/27669155/"},{"label":"Rudd2015","pmid":"25933358","proposed_action":"Remove from pubmed_phase_ii_iii_rct_links with user approval; retain as cardiac-safety support if a separate safety-source field exists.","rationale":"This is a pooled cardiac safety analysis of clinical-trial data, not a primary phase II/III placebo-controlled seizure-efficacy RCT report.","status":"not_phase_ii_iii","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/25933358/"},{"label":"Chung2010","pmid":"20132285","proposed_action":"Retain.","rationale":"Drug is lacosamide; randomized controlled adjunctive trial for partial-onset seizures with placebo arm and extractable 400 mg/day efficacy outcomes.","status":"verified","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/20132285/"},{"label":"Halasz2009","pmid":"19183227","proposed_action":"Retain.","rationale":"Drug is lacosamide; randomized placebo-controlled adjunctive partial-onset seizure trial with extractable 400 mg/day outcomes.","status":"verified","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/19183227/"},{"label":"BenMenachem2007","pmid":"17635557","proposed_action":"Retain.","rationale":"Drug is lacosamide; multicenter double-blind placebo-controlled adult partial-onset seizure trial with extractable 400 mg/day outcomes.","status":"verified","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/17635557/"}],"source_updates":[{"current_value":"FDA/DailyMed labeling","field":"mechanism_source","proposed_value":"FDA labeling","reason":"Mechanism is supported by FDA labeling; DailyMed wording should be avoided in source fields when trusted FDA/accessdata/openFDA sources are available.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/216185s001lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"FDA/DailyMed SPL; status=no_boxed_warning_in_selected_label...","field":"fda_black_box_warning_source","proposed_value":"FDA/openFDA drug label API; status=no_boxed_warning_identified_in_selected_current_fda_labeling; api_urls=https://api.fda.gov/drug/label.json?search=openfda.brand_name%3A%22VIMPAT%22&limit=10 and https://api.fda.gov/drug/label.json?search=openfda.brand_name%3A%22MOTPOLY%20XR%22&limit=10","reason":"Black-box warning verification must use FDA/openFDA/Drugs@FDA/accessdata, not DailyMed.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://api.fda.gov/drug/label.json?search=openfda.brand_name%3A%22VIMPAT%22&limit=10","https://api.fda.gov/drug/label.json?search=openfda.brand_name%3A%22MOTPOLY%20XR%22&limit=10"]},{"current_value":"PubMed loop 26/65 on 2026-05-15: 9 qualifying placebo-controlled randomized clinical trial report(s) retained from 26 PubMed candidate(s). Links were rebuilt from fetched PubMed PMID metadata and named FirstAuthorYear. Differential effectiveness columns summarize extractable maximum effective dose/regimen values within qualifying RCT reports.","field":"rct_pubmed_verification_notes","proposed_value":"Manual audit on 2026-05-20: retained Makedonska2024, Vossler2020, Farkas2019, Hong2016, Chung2010, Halasz2009, and BenMenachem2007 as qualifying lacosamide placebo-controlled phase II/III seizure-efficacy RCT reports. FoldvarySchaefer2017 is Phase IV sleepiness/cognition and Rudd2015 is pooled cardiac safety, so both require user approval before removal from the phase II/III RCT link field. Do not add Biton2015 as a missing RCT because it is a pooled safety/tolerability analysis of already represented trials, not an independent primary efficacy RCT.","reason":"Updates automated notes after manual concordance review.","requires_user_approval":true,"source_urls":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/28866338/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/25933358/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/26414341/"]}],"summary":"Lacosamide row is mostly correct for identity, US availability, FDA approval year, indications, dosing, mechanism, half-life, metabolism, QT/PR facts, and RR50/seizure-freedom outcomes. Updates are needed for FDA boxed-warning sourcing, trusted evidence source names, alias completeness, contradictory enzyme/QT filters, IV-only formulation wording, two non-qualifying RCT links, and the median-percent-change field because Makedonska2024's 3.2% value is not a median percent-change differential."}
